            <ArticleTitle>The Ethics of Big Data and Nursing Science.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-302</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0894318417724474</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Big data is a scientific, social, and technological trend referring to the process and size of datasets available for analysis. Ethical implications arise as healthcare disciplines, including nursing, struggle over questions of informed consent, privacy, ownership of data, and its possible use in epistemology. The author offers straight-thinking possibilities for the use of big data in nursing science.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
